Z||000003||SCCA FIERO||07-13-99||08:38 PM||||UMMMM....I have an idea Cliff. SLOW DOWN...LOL<p>I owned my 86 Feiro for 10 years and it never happened until about 2 months ago. One day I was on the freeway and hit about 90mph or so and was passing a big truck. The truck must have stirred up the wind and BAM!!! I almost crashed!!! I have had that Fiero way past 90 many times before and that never happened. It only happened that one time and it was the passenger light.<p>What about a chain attatched to the plastic on the bottom of the light unit,the part that rises with the lights. Hook one end to that and the other to the lid? It would allow the light to rise,but not unless the lights are on.
Z||000004||Cooter||07-13-99||10:04 PM||||My car wont go fast enough to make the lids pop up. Oh well, at least I get good gas mileage. . .
Z||000005||batboy||07-13-99||10:31 PM||||I had my headlights pop up and then bang back shut once when I was doing 70 mph on a narrow two-lane road when a 18 wheeler truck went by going the other way. Made me jump, I wasn't expecting it.
Z||000006||fierowner||07-13-99||11:50 PM||||Same deal happened to me...I was flying down the interstate in my 84 SE probably at about 90 or so...The Drivers side headlight door opened and i thought my headlight was up too...boy i was scared my car was going to be one of those one headlight up one headlight down cars....I marveled at it a bit and my friend advised I slowed down....I took his advice :-)
